{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786795436607888149,"compiled_state":{"alias":"actinium-civic-needletail","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"e89f400b82da9e9213d7ecc5b815ede3c4b57bbb1e5393024715af505bc28e4c","event_uuid":"ff0c4bd7-b91c-48a0-a336-4cd1c06136f7","position":{"commit_sha":"a7f10697a6598592856fa49ebbfe679857f21d4f","position":"1786782916770291001-ff0c4bd7-b91c-48a0-a336-4cd1c06136f7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"10d7c0333a28ee25167b9c359da1c53042bd8a789d46cf72a90924a9767d3c81","event_uuid":"30d622f3-fa20-4625-8fad-4ec976fe9202","position":{"commit_sha":"77cc3d9e4d4f1481162354cbe58eb30ae8508e72","position":"1786782941181247001-30d622f3-fa20-4625-8fad-4ec976fe9202"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786782916770291001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"30d622f3-fa20-4625-8fad-4ec976fe9202","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5014-d0c6-5bbe-47fb"}],"description":"The 'main Gerrit Verified Gate' workflow's macOS pytest job has a post-test step 'Report and release macOS default-suite pytest tree' that runs 'rm -rf' over the pytest RAM-disk basetemp. The snapshot tests (tests covering .rebar/run_snapshots, e.g. test_snapshot_is_read_only, test_snapshot_extracts_tracked) legitimately create read-only snapshot trees (0555 dirs / 0444 files). On macOS BSD 'rm', files inside a read-only directory cannot be unlinked ('Permission denied'), so the directory stays 'Directory not empty' and the step exits 1 EVEN THOUGH pytest itself passed (13393 passed, 65 skipped). This is intermittent (depends on which worker/snapshots land on the RAM disk) and blocks the Verified vote for otherwise-green changes. Fix: make the cleanup 'chmod -R u+w' the tree before 'rm -rf' (or use 'chflags -R nouchg' + 'rm -rf'), mirroring how the snapshot tests' own teardown restores perms. Observed on change 1808 patchsets 1 and 2 (3 consecutive macOS runs); recent unrelated changes pass the same job, confirming it is environmental, not change-specific.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b5e6-a289-e51b-41b2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"macOS Verified-gate cleanup step fails on read-only run_snapshots dirs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ff0c4bd7-b91c-48a0-a336-4cd1c06136f7","30d622f3-fa20-4625-8fad-4ec976fe9202"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786795436607888149,"uuid":"0a6eaea8-f440-403b-b362-b4ea2daea9e1"}